      "text": "~600 CE: Gupta Empire collapsed ~550; fragmentation\n  ~606-647: Harsha's empire (short-lived unity, north India)\n  ~700-1200: REGIONAL KINGDOMS — the peninsula's complex era\n             North: Gurjara-Pratihara, Rashtrakuta, Pala\n             South: Chalukya, Rashtrakuta, Chola (dominant)\n             Deccan: multiple competing dynasties\n  ~1000-1200: Mahmud of Ghazni raids; Ghurids conquer north\n  1206: DELHI SULTANATE begins — five dynasties, 320 years\n  1336: VIJAYANAGARA founded — last great Hindu empire\n  1526: MUGHAL EMPIRE begins (Babur)\n  1556-1605: Akbar — Mughal peak of coherent administration\n  1658-1707: Aurangzeb — expansion + religious reversal\n  1680s+: MARATHA CONFEDERACY rises; Mughal decline"
    },
